base.py,myenv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_core/runnables/base.py,4fbb1f96201d6df9f9df92383ced1f033fd64ee0,DavidRosario26387/ABEX_Multi-Agent-SEO-Blog-Generator,https://api.github.com/repositories/953538737/contents/myenv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_core/runnables/base.py?ref=18d37350b21894945b10eb9d4a336b3203b59ddc,https://api.github.com/repositories/953538737/git/blobs/4fbb1f96201d6df9f9df92383ced1f033fd64ee0,https://github.com/DavidRosario26387/ABEX_Multi-Agent-SEO-Blog-Generator/blob/18d37350b21894945b10eb9d4a336b3203b59ddc/myenv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_core/runnables/base.py,A Multi-Agent Blog Generator using the LangChain Framework,,0,0,0,4,2025-08-01T18:16:14Z,0,0,"# Multi-Agent Blog Generator using LangChain

### Overview
This project is a multi-agent blog generation system using the LangChain framework. It automates:
1. Researching a trend
2. Generating structured blog outlines
3. Creating blog content
4. Enhancing with SEO optimization
5. Proofreading for clarity and readability

### Key Highlights:

* LLMs (Llama 3-8B via Groq API) for AI-powered blog generation
* Serper API for real-time HR trend research
* LangChain agents for an autonomous workflow
* Streamlit UI for real-time progress tracking

### Tools & Frameworks Used
> python 3.10+ – Core language

> langChain – Multi-agent workflow execution

> Streamlit – UI for real-time progress updates

> Groq API (Llama 3-8B) – AI-powered blog content generation

> Serper API – Fetches HR trends from Google

> dotenv – Secure API key management

### Installation & Setup
1. Clone the Repository
```
git clone https://github.com/DavidRosario26387/ABEX_Multi-Agent-SEO-Blog-Generator.git
cd project
```
2. Create a Virtual Environment
```
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # Mac/Linux
venv\Scripts\activate      # Windows
```
3. Install Dependencies
```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
4. Set Up API Keys
> Create a .env file in the project root and add:
```
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key
SERPER_API_KEY=your_serper_api_key
```
5. Run the Application
```
streamlit run app.py
```

> Project Structure
```
project/
│── app.py               
│── blog_pipeline.py      
│── agents.py            
│── utils.py             
│── config.py             
│── requirements.txt     
│── .env                
```
