langchain_app.py,app/core/langchain_app.py,e3bf909ca09dae455a65b943bcde60f5ff6c0ad9,vijaykalore/DeployFlow---CI-CD-for-Gen-AI-Apps-on-AWS,https://api.github.com/repositories/1045769712/contents/app/core/langchain_app.py?ref=cad22f78214716f68a0f7d5fad3f68b3495911b9,https://api.github.com/repositories/1045769712/git/blobs/e3bf909ca09dae455a65b943bcde60f5ff6c0ad9,https://github.com/vijaykalore/DeployFlow---CI-CD-for-Gen-AI-Apps-on-AWS/blob/cad22f78214716f68a0f7d5fad3f68b3495911b9/app/core/langchain_app.py,,,0,0,0,1,2025-08-27T17:45:28Z,0,0,"# DeployFlow - CI/CD for Gen AI Apps on AWS

DeployFlow is a reference CI/CD pipeline and sample FastAPI app targeting generative AI workloads (FastAPI + optional LangChain) with AWS ECR/ECS deployment.

This repo implements the LLD/HLD you provided:
- API Service (FastAPI) to trigger and inspect pipelines
- Pipeline Orchestrator (CICDPipeline) that builds, tests, deploys, and notifies
- AI App Module (LangChainApp stub) for model logic
- AWS Integration (scripts + stubbed class) to push image and deploy to ECS
- Test Runner (pytest + lightweight TestRunner)

## Quick start

- Local API: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`
- Trigger pipeline: POST `/pipeline/trigger` then GET `/pipeline/status/{run_id}`
- Run tests: `pytest -q`
- Build image: `docker build -t deployflow:local .`

## Requirements
- Python 3.10+
- pip
- Docker (for container build)
- AWS CLI v2 (for deploy)

## AWS Deploy (ECR + ECS)
Use one of the scripts (Linux/macOS or Windows PowerShell):
- `scripts/deploy_to_aws.sh`
- `scripts/deploy_to_aws.ps1`

Required env vars:
- `AWS_REGION` (e.g., us-east-1)
- `AWS_ACCOUNT_ID`
- `ECR_REPOSITORY` (e.g., deployflow)
- `ECS_CLUSTER`
- `ECS_SERVICE`
- Optional: `IMAGE_TAG` (default: git sha or `latest`)

## GitHub Actions
A workflow is provided in `.github/workflows/deployflow-ci.yml` that:
- Installs dependencies and runs tests
- Builds and pushes an image to ECR (on main branch)
- Updates ECS service

Provide these GitHub secrets: `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_ACCOUNT_ID`, `ECR_REPOSITORY`, `ECS_CLUSTER`, `ECS_SERVICE`.

## Notes
- LangChain is optional; the app falls back to a stub if not installed.
- This is an educational scaffold. Harden for production (secrets, IAM, retries, rollbacks).
